{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability","id":1394844,"title":"Mapmaking Ability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T12:53:40-07:00","id":1394844,"title":"Mapmaking Ability","content":"One of my players is going for a Solar Cartographer to be part of our game in the West, and I'm not totally sure where mapmaking should sit as an ability. Linguistics has a few things that would work (Whirling Brush Method explicitly references it), but it feels more Craft as an ability to me, even though there's no real mechanical hooks in the tree for it.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on how to handle this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T13:26:09-07:00","id":1394845,"title":"","content":"Seems to me like it would fall under Lore most naturally, the Ability for most non-Occult learning. Unless it's naval navigational charts (which might be just as appropriate in the West), in which case you might also substitute Sail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T13:37:03-07:00","id":1394846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability#post1394844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players is going for a Solar Cartographer to be part of our game in the West, and I'm not totally sure where mapmaking should sit as an ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Linguistics. There's actually a sidebar in the corebook on this subject (&quot;Artistic Talent: Linguistics or Craft?&quot;, Exalted p. 323), which states &quot;Very specific forms of art are also constructs of language: maps, diagrams, and supplemental illustrations fall into these categories. Where art is concerned, Linguistics mainly provides the ability to produce beautiful and complex letters, and extremely complex, detailed informational illustrations.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T13:59:12-07:00","id":1394849,"title":"","content":"OK, so that clarifies my gut instinct. So would it be simply that making a map is a Linguistics roll, or are particularly complex maps &quot;Linguistics projects&quot;? Part of me wonders if the latter is overcomplicating things, but I'd also like the possibility of magical maps to be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:01:10-07:00","id":1394919,"title":"","content":"Magical maps should be the products of sorcerous workings rather than artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T06:23:45-07:00","id":1395066,"title":"","content":"As in the quote, Linguistics is the ability of conveying information, while Craft is the ability of making stuff. As such the rules have some flex so that you can be a caligrapher with just Linguistics, mostly because genre tropes. Lore also has a role here since without it you may not know what information you're supposed to convey.<br /> <br /> Since it matters to your story*, I would say:<br /> - Linguistics alone is enough to produce accurate, potentially beautiful maps of a territory that you personally know well or are actively looking at. Materials don't matter; could be ink on vellum, or scratches on birchbark. A really complex map (i.e. an atlas) might be an extended Linguistics roll (like a novel), a bunch of independent rolls (like a collection of poems), or some combination of the two. Wing this based on which feels more situationally appropriate/dramatic.<br /> - If you want your map or atlas to be especially durable, or an otherwise well-made, valuable object above and beyond the information it contains or its beauty as art, that's a Craft project, with the Linguistics pieces as ingredients.<br /> - If you want to compile relevant information about a territory so that you can make a map sight-unseen, use Lore. Use Investigation and social Abilities to collect information directly from locals, travelers, or others with first-hand experience. If you want to survey the area yourself, use Survival (on land) or Sail (for coastlines). Each of these approaches comes with interesting potential for inclusions and omissions.<br /> <br /> * If making a map is just something that comes up once in passing and isn't a major plot thread, but success vs. failure was still meaningful, I'd probably just get by on a single roll of whatever Ability aligned best with why we were bothering to roll it in the first place. E.g. the scout wants to make a map of the territory ahead for the general, so he rolls Survival to make sure he doesn't leave out any major hazards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-08-2020, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T10:58:28-07:00","id":1395109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1394919#post1394919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magical maps should be the products of sorcerous workings rather than artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> ten characters, oh yeah!</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:56:38-07:00","id":1395133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1394849#post1394849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be simply that making a map is a Linguistics roll, or are particularly complex maps &quot;Linguistics projects&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that any single map that covered less than all of Creation would probably be just a single roll rather than a project. But a bundle of charts could very well be an extended roll, just like writing a novel is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like the possibility of magical maps to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Linguistics can definitely make magical maps, to the same degree it can produce magical books/letters/pamphlets. Several of the existing Linguistics charms should work just fine on maps. Letter-Within-A-Letter Technique, for instance, could make a map that conveyed, to the right person, a completely different message, whether that was a totally different map, or something totally cartographically unrelated. I'd allow maps to convey social influence too, even without charms - I think a well-made map could quite reasonably justify instilling an Intimacy of some type towards the area it depicts, for example. <br /> <br /> You could also come up with some custom Linguistics charms specifically for map-making. One idea for that might be a charm that accurately conveys your knowledge of the terrain you're mapping, so that someone who reads the map would intuitively <i>see</i> the land, just as if they had been where you had been. Another one would be a map so visually obvious that it conveyed all its information without the need to share a language with the map-maker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:14:39-07:00","id":1395282,"title":"","content":"I feel like there should be a place for survival or sail in there somewhere. The bigger question is how big a deal will actual cartography be in the game. If it isn't going to be a huge issue let the player suggest what they think works and roll with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:25:54-07:00","id":1395369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1395282#post1395282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there should be a place for survival or sail in there somewhere. The bigger question is how big a deal will actual cartography be in the game. If it isn't going to be a huge issue let the player suggest what they think works and roll with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The latter part... remains to be seen. I want to work it in somewhere, but it may take a while. I'm a little hesitant to leave it to the player as she's new to Storyteller in general, let alone Exalted. Trying to keep as much of the &quot;heavy lifting &quot; on my side as possible.<br /> <br /> I don't see it being too huge to start with (they're loitering around Lathe, for the most part), but it could grow quite happily as they need to hunt stuff down. There are several reasons for them to go further West baked into the plot so far.<br /> <br /> Involving Survival and Sail... maybe. Having some way of tracking where you are, how fast you're going, what you're seeing etc, should be part of that. Potentially have the difficulty of the cartography impacted by the initial Sail or Survival (Navigation) roll to go through the terrain in the first place? Otherwise you're working off other maps, and so things like Lore would apply, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> has suggested. I think that framework as a whole would work really well.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily want it tied to any Sail or Survival roll made by the mapmaker themselves; several famous navigators/explorers in real-world history had local guides to get them from A to B while they charted and observed. If they're the ones doing it then fine, but having it be &quot;the roll made to navigate the party&quot; rather than &quot;the roll the mapmaker makes&quot; makes the most sense to me.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the suggestions so far, very helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:11:01-07:00","id":1395481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1395109#post1395109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> ten characters, oh yeah!</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Because to me, a magical map seems too stand-alone to be an artifact; it just does a thing, it doesn't act as an extension of its reader's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T00:28:09-07:00","id":1395538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1395481#post1395481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because to me, a magical map seems too stand-alone to be an artifact; it just does a thing, it doesn't act as an extension of its reader's power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depend on what it does. If you can put your finger on it and get s vision of the place it depicts, or have a map that changes so that the traveller is always at the centre of the map, are either of those an artefact?<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that artefacts do not have to have evocations in order to be artefacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T21:06:47-07:00","id":1395756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394844-mapmaking-ability?p=1395538#post1395538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can put your finger on it and get s vision of the place it depicts, or have a map that changes so that the traveller is always at the centre of the map, are either of those an artefact?</div> </div> </div> </div>As described, I'd say no. Those both feel like just the kind of straightforward enchanted objects that Workings are good for. Which, let's not forget, can also create fully sentient beings, so it's not exactly a &quot;power level&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Edit for additional thought: The first one I think is 100% better suited to a Working. The map is essentially a portable magic window to a specific place. The details (how big a place, how much resolution) would set the scope and ambition. Probably high finesse to get a nice, neat, rolled-up-parchment map.<br /> <br /> The second... I still think would work better as a Working, but it's closer to the line. It wouldn't take much (e.g., combining it with the clairvoyance power of the first example) before it would feel more Artifact-y to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-11-2020, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T20:02:49-07:00","id":1395960,"title":"","content":"So mostly because the magical maps your imagining are closer to what you'd expect to produce with a working than what you'd expect to get from crafting.<br /> <br /> I suspect that if I asked people to come up with an artifact ** map that was clearly an artifact folks would be able to come up with an idea or two that would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> In fact Xerxes' examples feel more like artifacts to my sensibilities (but if the first map was carved in a stone floor of a manse/cave/temple and immobile it would seem more working like).<br /> <br /> My sense of the thematic split is that workings are things that <u>are</u> a bit of magic or the products of that magic, while artifacts are things that <u>do</u> magic. I can imagine maps that fit in either category.<br /> <br /> Here's my first crack at an artifact map<br /> <br /> <b>Cartographer's paper, artifact *</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">This 1 meter square sheet of vellum with ornately embroidered fabric borders, when created is blank with except for a single dot of ink drawn some place on the page by it's creator. The paper can be attuned for 2 motes. The person attuned to the map can, through concentration, cause any landmark that they see to be inked into the parchment. The small dot on the parchment represents the location of the attuned user when the first landmark was inked into the page. When the user attempts to mark the location of a landmark that falls outside of the boundaries of the map as it exists, the entire marked area of the map shrinks to resize itself into scale that can fit the greater extent required to include the new landmark. The location of the original dot always stays the same and the orientation of the map is always constant. Typically the elemental poles are embroidered into the fabric border for reference but not always.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 06-11-2020, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}